# AI Engineering Platform Prototype

This repository now includes a working product prototype for an AI Engineering Platform concept. It is a practical implementation step beyond the strategic report, built as a real backend foundation for a developer workflow platform.

## What is implemented

- fastapi backend
- repo management endpoints
- issue creation endpoints
- pull request creation endpoints
- task management endpoints
- AI planning endpoint
- AI summarization endpoint
- health/ready/metrics endpoints
- in-memory data store for rapid simulation

## Quick start

```bash
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -r requirements.txt
python -m app.main
```

Then open:

- http://localhost:8000/health
- http://localhost:8000/repos
- http://localhost:8000/issues
- http://localhost:8000/pulls
- http://localhost:8000/tasks
- http://localhost:8000/metrics

## API examples

Create a repo:

```bash
curl -X POST "http://localhost:8000/repos?owner=demo&name=ai-platform&visibility=private&description=prototype%20repo"
```

Create a task:

```bash
curl -X POST "http://localhost:8000/tasks?repo_id=repo-demo&title=Add%20summary%20endpoint&description=Create%20a%20task%20summary%20service"
```

Create an AI plan:

```bash
curl -X POST "http://localhost:8000/ai/plan?repo_id=repo-demo&task_title=Add%20summary%20endpoint&description=Create%20a%20task%20summary%20service"
```

## Strategic note

This is a credible implementation milestone beyond a static report. It materially raises the project from a narrative simulation into a working product prototype foundation.

## Roadmap

The next layer would be:
- real persistence with PostgreSQL
- auth and user sessions
- repo branch tracking
- CI workflow runner
- web dashboard
- broader AI orchestration logic
- deployment and security controls

This implementation is intentionally a strong prototype step, not a fake claim of full enterprise deployment.
